            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-55132-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-55132 medium vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw in Node.js's permission model allows a file's access and modification timestamps to be changed via `futimes()` even when the process has only read permissions. Unlike `utimes()`, `futimes()` does not apply the expected write-permission checks, which means file metadata can be modified in read-only directories. This behavior could be used to alter timestamps in ways that obscure activity, reducing the reliability of logs. This vulnerability affects users of the permission model on Node.js v20,  v22,  v24, and v25."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-55132\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: node\nVersion: 22.21.1\nFix Version: 20.20.0,22.22.0,24.13.0,25.3.0\nType: binary\nLocation: /nodejs/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-55132](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-55132)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-55132**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | node  | 22.21.1  | 20.20.0,22.22.0,24.13.0,25.3.0  | binary  | /nodejs/bin/node  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-55132](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-55132)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-59465-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-59465 high vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A malformed `HTTP/2 HEADERS` frame with oversized, invalid `HPACK` data can cause Node.js to crash by triggering an unhandled `TLSSocket` error `ECONNRESET`. Instead of safely closing the connection, the process crashes, enabling a remote denial of service. This primarily affects applications that do not attach explicit error handlers to secure sockets, for example:\n```\nserver.on('secureConnection', socket =\u003e {\n  socket.on('error', err =\u003e {\n    console.log(err)\n  })\n})\n```"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-59465\nSeverity: high\nPackage: node\nVersion: 22.21.1\nFix Version: 20.20.0,22.22.0,24.13.0,25.3.0\nType: binary\nLocation: /nodejs/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-59465](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-59465)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-59465**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | node  | 22.21.1  | 20.20.0,22.22.0,24.13.0,25.3.0  | binary  | /nodejs/bin/node  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-59465](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-59465)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-59466-node",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-59466 high vulnerability for node package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "We have identified a bug in Node.js error handling where \"Maximum call stack size exceeded\" errors become uncatchable when `async_hooks.createHook()` is enabled. Instead of reaching `process.on('uncaughtException')`, the process terminates, making the crash unrecoverable. Applications that rely on `AsyncLocalStorage` (v22, v20) or `async_hooks.createHook()` (v24, v22, v20) become vulnerable to denial-of-service crashes triggered by deep recursion under specific conditions."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-59466\nSeverity: high\nPackage: node\nVersion: 22.21.1\nFix Version: 20.20.0,22.22.0,24.13.0,25.3.0\nType: binary\nLocation: /nodejs/bin/node\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-59466](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-59466)",
